{
  "name": "require_fields timezone_resolvable: unresolvable zones are DROPPED, not fatal",
  "why": "In PostgreSQL 16, AT TIME ZONE on a zone the server does not know ABORTS THE QUERY \u2014 it does not skip the row \u2014 so an adapter that renders this naively turns one browser-supplied junk zone into zero results for the whole scan. Dropping is the only behaviour that degrades safely. Two of the five rows survive: the modern spelling, and a LEGACY alias, because one legacy zone name covered 133 production sessions and was invisible to every timezone rule that listed only the modern one. The empty-string zone and the absent zone take DIFFERENT code paths and both must drop.",
